# JetStream Example
# This file demonstrates how to use the new JetStream features in the NATS client.

# Define variables for reuse
@url = nats://localhost:4222
@stream = orders
@subject = orders.new
@consumer = monitor

# 1. Publish a message to a JetStream stream
# The JSPUBLISH command ensures the message is persisted.
JSPUBLISH {{url}}/{{subject}}
NATS-Stream: {{stream}}

{
  "id": "order-123",
  "status": "created"
}

###

# 2. Consume from a JetStream consumer
# This will start consuming from the specified stream and consumer.
# You can use the path syntax: stream/consumer
JSCONSUME {{url}}/{{stream}}/{{consumer}}

###

# 3. Consume using metadata headers
# Alternatively, you can specify stream and durable name in headers.
JSCONSUME {{url}}
NATS-Stream: {{stream}}
NATS-Durable: {{consumer}}
